"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about actions that were completed in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use both regular and irregular past tense verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Regular verbs end in<span class=\"italic\"> -ed</span>, while irregular ones do not. Some follow patterns, others do not. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be - was/were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It was  March in South Africa and the marula were ripe.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wander - wandered<br/>drink - drank\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">A small herd of elephants wandered in at night and drank more than 100 gallons of homemade mahua alcohol.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spend - spent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They spent a long time devouring the sweet pulp and tangy skin. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Continuous  (reactions/behaviors)", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For Past Continuous, we add was/were + verb \u201cing\u201d. <br/>Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add \u201cing\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grow - was/were growing<br/>ferment - was/were fermenting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In fact much of it, growing wild, was fermenting in the sun.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"weave - was/were weaving<br/>fall - was/were falling\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Suddenly they were weaving, stumbling and falling all over each other.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lie - was/were lying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He  took pictures of the calves and adults that were lying in a contented pile.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Often you use the Simple Past tense and the Past Continuous tense in sentences together. The long action (Past Continuous) is interrupted by a short action (Simple Past).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When they were done they started pushing their way into homes. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A field guide who was driving through the area stopped. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Thousands of the oval yellow fruit were lying on the forest floor when the elephants discovered them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many of the villagers were sleeping when they heard the intoxicated animals crashing through their walls.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They were still waiting for the elephants to move away from their flattened dwellings a few hours later when the sun came up.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "marula", "type": "name"}, {"content": "typical fruits from South Africa ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was March in South Africa and the marula were ripe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about drunk elephants.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ripe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fully mature and ready to eat", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was March in South Africa and the marula were ripe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to ferment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go through a chemical change that results in the production of alcohol", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The marula were fermenting in the sun.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pulp", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the soft, juicy part of a fruit ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The elephants spent a long time devouring the sweet pulp and tangy skin.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to devour", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to quickly eat in a way that shows that you are very hungry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The elephants spent a long time devouring the sweet pulp and tangy skin.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tangy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a strong taste", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The elephants spent a long time devouring the sweet pulp and tangy skin.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to weave", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move from side to side while going forward; not able to walk in a straight line", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Suddenly the drunk elephants were weaving, stumbling and falling all over each other. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to stumble", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to hit your foot on something when you are walking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Suddenly the drunk elephants were weaving, stumbling and falling all over each other. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to catch a whiff of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to sense the smell or odor of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He caught a whiff of the fermented fruit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob02aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "intoxicated", "type": "name"}, {"content": "affected by alcohol or drugs", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The villagers were sleeping when they heard the intoxicated animals crashing through their walls.", "type": "ex